Interpretation
--------------
- 8 test files, 61 test functions, 8 files failing, 0 passing — the intended
  red baseline: the tests fail because the stubs call
  `abort("MojoAkku: this API is not yet implemented")`, not for any other reason.
- Edge cases derived from the docs are covered explicitly: EMPTY, INVALID_FORMAT
  (partial/extra component, `v`/`=` prefix, whitespace, empty identifiers,
  double separators), LEADING_ZERO (core and numeric prerelease), BAD_NUMBER,
  OVERFLOW, build leading-zero allowance, build-ignored precedence and equality,
  the full semver.org item-11 chain, and antisymmetry.
- The tests are expected to go green in Phase 11 (implementation).
